  uidb64: MQ
  token: cs1234-a0b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1a2b3c4d5
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  Not an API call -- the URL dj-rest-auth reverses when building the
  password-reset link. `AccountAdapter` rewrites the emailed link to the
  frontend, so this route is normally never hit.

  It used to be a bare `TemplateView` with no template configured, which returned
  a **500** to anyone who did follow it. It now 302s to
  `{{frontend_url}}/auth/password/reset/confirm/<uid>/<token>`.

  The frontend then posts uid, token and the new password to
  `POST /rest-auth/password/reset/confirm/` -- see
  **forgot password > reset password**.

  ## API example response
  302 Location: {{frontend_url}}/auth/password/reset/confirm/MQ/<token>
}
